# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./xymon-plugin at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi-rag
version: 0.2.0
summary: a search of Xymon's manual pages and history by meaning; the index task on the server, search and ask anywhere
server-short: the search index, kept up to date
tools-short: search by meaning, from here
data: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/xymonapi-rag/
requires: xymonapi >= 8.0.0 (its client beside it; the API beside it on the server, over the network elsewhere), python >= 3.9
manual: xymonapi-rag.1

# How ./xymon-plugin installs it: see xymonapi's PLUGIN file.
server-needs: xymonapi
tools-needs: xymonapi
server-files: xymonrag.py xymonapi-rag.sh requirements.txt
server-manual: xymonapi-rag.1
server-modules: fastembed numpy
task: xymonapi-rag.tasks.DIST
uninstalled: Uninstalled xymonapi-rag. Kept: its index, $XYMONAPI_RAG_INDEX, and xymonapi.
tools-files: xymonrag.py xymonapi-rag.sh requirements.txt
tools-manual: xymonapi-rag.1
tools-optional-modules: fastembed numpy
venv-note: only to keep an index on this machine: search and ask through the server need none
command: xymonapi-rag xymonapi-rag.sh
executable: xymonapi-rag.sh
installed-tools: It searches the API xymonapi-connect connected this machine to, or XYMONAPI_URL, when there is no index here.
uninstalled-tools: Uninstalled xymonapi-rag. Kept: xymonapi's client, and any index here, $XYMONAPI_RAG_INDEX.
